<article class="env-remark" id="03F3">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03F3">Remark <span data-tag="03F3">7.1.2.6</span> <span class="named">(Powers as Limits)</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category containing objects $X$ and $Y$. Then a morphism of simplicial sets $e: K \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(X,Y)$ can be identified with a natural transformation $\alpha : \underline{X} \rightarrow \underline{Y}$, where $\underline{X}, \underline{Y}: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ denote the constant diagrams taking the values $X$ and $Y$, respectively. In this case: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The natural transformation $\alpha $ exhibits the object $X$ as a limit of the diagram $\underline{Y}$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="02VZ" href="/tag/02VZ">7.1.1.1</a>) if and only if $e$ exhibits $X$ as a power of $Y$ by $K$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="03EY" href="/tag/03EY">7.1.2.1</a>). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The natural transformation $\alpha $ exhibits the object $Y$ as a colimit of the diagram $\underline{X}$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="02VZ" href="/tag/02VZ">7.1.1.1</a>) if and only if $e$ exhibits $Y$ as a copower of $X$ by $K$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="03EY" href="/tag/03EY">7.1.2.1</a>). 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
